Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `holder.res` was consumed by `holder.res.move()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/ownership/holder_field_partial_move_is_recorded.jet:15:22
    |
 15 |     print(holder.res.name)
    |                      ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/ownership/holder_field_partial_move_is_recorded.jet:14:10
    |
 14 |     grab(holder.res.move())
    |          ^^^^^^^^^^ `holder.res` moved to `holder.res.move()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `holder.res` after the move, or give `holder.res.move()` a copy with `holder.res.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
